{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_q6yzqndkfbpjcximjzsdpjcrfnc2hrq4wkwfp3htklirqf77ag5q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the C-to-Rust translation in `src/inversion_list.rs`:\n\n**Core operations** (`new`, `capacity`, `support`, `contains`, `clone_list`, `complement`, `to_str`):\n- `new` builds half-open intervals from sorted/deduped values, errors with `ValueOutOfRange` when distinct values can't fit in capacity, otherwise treats out-of-range values as a \"NULL\"-equivalent (empty) set — mirroring how the C library returns NULL.\n- `complement` walks the gaps between intervals within `[0, capacity)`.\n\n**Set comparisons** (`equal`, `is_strict_subset_of`, `is_subset_of`, `is_disjoint`):\n- I faithfully reproduce the C's quirky `inversion_list_less` semantics (which is mapped to `is_strict_subset_of` per the test's mapping comment).\n- `is_disjoint` mirrors the C's odd implementation as `not_equal`.\n\n**Set operations** (`union`, `intersection`, `difference`, `symmetric_difference`):\n- Each handles empty operands as \"identity\" (matching the C's NULL-handling), so chained calls behave correctly even when an intermediate `new` produced an empty set.\n- `symmetric_difference` is computed as `(A ∪ B) \\ (A ∩ B)`.\n\n**Iterators** (`InversionListIterator`, `InversionListCoupleIterator`):\n- The element iterator walks through each interval's range; the couple iterator yields `(lo, hi)` pairs.\n\nAll 15 tests pass under `cargo test` within the 60-second budget."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1570,"cache_read_input_tokens":79575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1570,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba31